{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Self-Attention from Scratch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Softmax from scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Softmax converts raw logits into probabilities. Subtract the max for numerical stability."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def softmax(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    shifted = x - np.max(x, axis=-1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    exp_x = np.exp(shifted)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return exp_x / np.sum(exp_x, axis=-1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "logits = np.array([2.0, 1.0, 0.1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"logits:  {logits}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"softmax: {softmax(logits)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"sum:     {softmax(logits).sum():.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Scaled dot-product attention"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The core function. Takes Q, K, V matrices and returns the attention output plus the weight matrix."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def scaled_dot_product_attention(Q, K, V):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dk = Q.shape[-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scores = Q @ K.T / np.sqrt(dk)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    weights = softmax(scores)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    output = weights @ V"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return output, weights"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Self-attention class with learned projections"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A full self-attention module with Wq, Wk, Wv weight matrices initialized with Xavier-like scaling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class SelfAttention:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, d_model, dk, dv, seed=42):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        scale = np.sqrt(2.0 / (d_model + dk))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.Wq = rng.normal(0, scale, (d_model, dk))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.Wk = rng.normal(0, scale, (d_model, dk))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        scale_v = np.sqrt(2.0 / (d_model + dv))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.Wv = rng.normal(0, scale_v, (d_model, dv))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.dk = dk"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        Q = X @ self.Wq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        K = X @ self.Wk"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        V = X @ self.Wv"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        output, weights = scaled_dot_product_attention(Q, K, V)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return output, weights"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Run it on a sentence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Create fake embeddings for a sentence and watch the attention weights."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "sentence = [\"The\", \"cat\", \"sat\", \"on\", \"the\", \"mat\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "n_tokens = len(sentence)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "d_model = 8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dk = 4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dv = 4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "rng = np.random.default_rng(42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X = rng.normal(0, 1, (n_tokens, d_model))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "attn = SelfAttention(d_model, dk, dv, seed=42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "output, weights = attn.forward(X)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"Attention weights (each row: where that token looks):\\n\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"{'':>6}\", end=\"\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for token in sentence:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"{token:>6}\", end=\"\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for i, token in enumerate(sentence):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"{token:>6}\", end=\"\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for j in range(n_tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        w = weights[i][j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"{w:6.3f}\", end=\"\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Visualize attention with ASCII heatmap"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Map attention weights to characters for a quick visual."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def ascii_heatmap(weights, tokens, chars=\" \u2591\u2592\u2593\u2588\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"\\n{'':>6}\", end=\"\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for t in tokens:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"{t:>6}\", end=\"\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"{tokens[i]:>6}\", end=\"\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            level = int(weights[i][j] * (len(chars) - 1) / weights.max())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            level = min(level, len(chars) - 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            print(f\"{'  ' + chars[level] + '   '}\", end=\"\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ascii_heatmap(weights, sentence)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Modify `scaled_dot_product_attention` to accept an optional mask matrix that sets certain positions to negative infinity before softmax (this is how causal/decoder masking works)\n2. Implement multi-head attention from scratch: split Q, K, V into `n_heads` chunks, run attention on each, concatenate, and project through a final weight matrix Wo\n3. Take two different sentences of the same length, feed them through the same SelfAttention instance, and compare their attention patterns. What changes? What stays the same?"
      ]
    }
